  "scoring_semantics": {
    "formula": "composite = prefill_gain ^ 0.25 * decode_gain ^ 0.75. Per component: gain = control / candidate per-token time (serial-anchored -- a faster candidate scores > 1). Decode per-token time is the decode window: decode-run time / N, with no seed prefill in it. The run is PAIRED on the box: official_pairs pairs, each one serial-control leg on the organizer-staged reference tree and one candidate leg, single-stream (serial only -- this track declares no speculative arm). Pair k measures live_goldens[(k - 1) mod N], so each live golden gets the same number of pairs. The score is the mean of the per-pair composites (official_pair_combine: mean). Floors and the ceilings apply to every pair."
  },
